A||||4||Brandon86SE||Help!  I'm pissing coolant!||||9||
Z||000000||Brandon86SE||11-14-2001||05:44 PM||||I haven't been able to drive my car for 5 days 'cause my back has been so bad, but today I took it to the chiropractors and back.  When I got back I heard something dripping under the engine.  So I took a look (as best as I could) under the car, and sure enough it was a steady stream of coolant coming out, then after a few seconds it slowed to a drizzle, and finally stopped.  What irks me is that this is coming out on the driver side of the engine.  In the last coulpe weeks I have been doing some work on the car, and on one such occasion had to remove the big hose going to the rad-cap.  But this is on the passenger side of the engine, and everything felt tight with the hose.  Although it did have a slight bit of moisture under the connecting point next to the battery ground.  I'm not sure what would be leaking that much on the driver side.  If anyone has some suggestions I would appreciate it.  I would do some more searching around in the engine myself for the source, but can't right now.  A visual inspection from overhead didn't reveal anything particularly obvious.<P>Thanks,<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||California Kid||11-14-2001||06:06 PM||||If the hose's and connections look good, check the engine block, there are round metal "freeze plugs" on the block that maybe one of them corroded through. Easy to fix, but you have to get completely under the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voytek||11-14-2001||06:29 PM||||Not too much stuff on the driver's side.  One of the hoses from the radiator does come up to the engine on that side but that's about it.<P>Other than that, plugs? or head gasket?  I hate to say the h/g words but it's a possibility.<P>Keep in mind, leaks don't always occur where they seem to come from.  I'd get underneath the car with a bright light - that should help.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||11-14-2001||07:25 PM||||If this is a V6 engine, and you are really lucky, the lines that circulate coolant thru the throttle body are leaking.  This would be an easy fix.  Good Luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brandon86SE||11-14-2001||07:35 PM||||ya, I guess I should specify what I have.  It's a stock 2.8 V6.  I hope I'm lucky.  don't even wanna think about the h/g thing.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
